<title>UK: Weather shuts off Novorossiisk, Ventspils oil port.</title>
<headline>Weather shuts off Novorossiisk, Ventspils oil port.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong winds and high swell have shut the main export points for Russian crude oil and products, a shipping source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The main Black Sea terminal at Novorrossiisk has been shut since 2130 local hours on Thursday after winds hit Gale Force 7 and swell rose to two metres, shipping inspector Petrak said.</p>
<p>At the time of the closure, there were three crude tankers at anchor and one tanker loaded with about a million barrels of Urals crude due to set sail.</p>
<p>High winds also hampered activity at the Latvian port of Ventspils where loading and berthing has been suspended since 0600 hours local on Friday.</p>
<p>There was one gas oil tanker alongside waiting to sail when the weather improves and three gas oil tankers, a gasoline tanker and a crude tanker at berth.</p>
<p>All other Russian seaborne export outlets were operating normally on Friday, Petrak said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 425 6280</p>
</text>
